  "notes": [
    "SBM parameterization: c_out=mu*cave, c_in=2*cave-c_out, p_in=c_in/N, p_out=c_out/N",
    "Detectability limit mu*=1-1/sqrt(cave)=0.5528 for cave=5.0",
    "BP uses full graph (no LCC). Embedding methods use LCC to avoid embcom issues.",
    "log(R+): only nonzero entries kept, floor at 1e-10 before log",
    "free_logR factorizes only nonzero positions (implicit negative PMI = missing)",
    "BP re-run with iters=5 (original run used iters=1, causing trivial fixed-point convergence in many cases)",
    "BP confirms community structure exists: NMI=0.56 at mu=0.3, 0.20 at mu=0.4, collapses ~mu=0.5",
    "BP failure at mu=0.5 may be finite-iters artifact; community structure IS present (node2vec finds it)",
    "SBM parameterization verified CORRECT: BP detects communities below mu*=0.553",
    "Critical findings: svd_R and free_R both fail (NMI~0.001) everywhere -- linear factorization of R is useless",
    "svd_logR (log+ortho) achieves NMI=0.25 at mu=0.3 and 0.023 at mu=0.4 -- log nonlinearity helps",
    "free_logR (log+free) underperforms svd_logR -- freedom from ortho does NOT help",
    "node2vec (N=500) achieves NMI=0.63/0.33/0.10 at mu=0.3/0.4/0.5 -- best overall",
    "Key conclusion: log nonlinearity is the most important factor. Free factorization does NOT help over SVD.",
    "node2vec superiority over free_logR likely comes from (c) stochastic gradient/noise regularization",
    "node2vec uses N=500 vs N=2000 for other methods -- results not directly comparable"
  ]
